    "body": "For lazy loaded iframes the intersection with the viewport cannot be determined here because it would have to be rendered first, right? As such we would never set the flag to `false` and it stays true.\n\nShould we remove this particular condition so that clients then wait for `browsingContext.load` only for the non-lazy case, and a lazy iframe that resumes shows up as a normal navigation later. Or should it maybe part of https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#process-the-iframe-attributes but that would defer the `WebDriver BiDi navigable created` invocation.",
